 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Sir Reginald painted five lighthouses plain white. Even the pigeon got lost.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.409
  },
  {
   "text": "He's the world's fanciest designer. Motto: \"Less is more!\" So why do lighthouses wear stripes?",
   "s": 4.609,
   "e": 9.596
  },
  {
   "text": "Puffin Coast had five: stripes, a spiral, checkers, polka dots, and one with a mustache.",
   "s": 9.896,
   "e": 14.566
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Tacky,\" said Sir Reginald. \"Less is more!\" By Tuesday, all five were white.",
   "s": 14.766,
   "e": 18.578
  },
  {
   "text": "Pip the intern raised her hand. \"Um, the stripes are...\" \"Less is more, Pip.\"",
   "s": 18.778,
   "e": 22.705
  },
  {
   "text": "So Captain Mo sailed in with four tons of cheese for Lighthouse Three.",
   "s": 22.825,
   "e": 26.31
  },
  {
   "text": "But in daylight the lamps are off. Five white towers. He picked one. Wrong.",
   "s": 26.51,
   "e": 29.916
  },
  {
   "text": "He unloaded the cheese for a keeper who hates cheese.",
   "s": 30.116,
   "e": 32.432
  },
  {
   "text": "By Friday, the mail boat, the ice cream boat and Sir Reginald's yacht were lost.",
   "s": 32.632,
   "e": 36.212
  },
  {
   "text": "Gary the pigeon landed on the wrong lighthouse eleven times. He wanted his nest.",
   "s": 36.412,
   "e": 40.722
  },
  {
   "text": "So what were the tacky stripes for?",
   "s": 40.922,
   "e": 42.349
  },
  {
   "text": "At night, every lighthouse blinks its own pattern. In daylight, the paint is the pattern.",
   "s": 42.649,
   "e": 46.753
  },
  {
   "text": "Stripes mean Lighthouse One. The spiral is Two, checkers Three, polka dots Four. Sailors read them like name tags, from three miles out.",
   "s": 46.953,
   "e": 54.692
  },
  {
   "text": "Pip repainted all five by Monday. Then a tugboat towed Sir Reginald home.",
   "s": 55.092,
   "e": 59.068
  },
  {
   "text": "And Gary flew straight to his nest. The one with the mustache.",
   "s": 59.268,
   "e": 62.308
  }
 ],
